---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Methane Outliers Map" path="/map/">
  <header class="masthead">
    <div>
      <h1>The most flared-and-vented, relative to production</h1>
      <p class="tagline">
        The top 50 reporting units in each jurisdiction &mdash; Alberta
        facilities, Texas leases &mdash; ranked by
        <strong>flared+vented gas as a share of gas-equivalent
        production</strong> over the same rolling 12-month window,
        computed the same way on both sides. Slide through four years
        of aligned windows. (Neither jurisdiction publishes complete
        well-level attribution; the reporting unit is as close as
        public data gets.)
      </p>
    </div>
    <span class="window-badge" id="window-badge" hidden></span>
  </header>

  <section class="tiles" id="tiles" aria-label="Window totals"></section>

  <div class="controls">
    <div class="slider-wrap">
      <label for="window-slider" id="slider-label">12 months ending &hellip;</label>
      <input type="range" id="window-slider" min="0" max="0" value="0" />
    </div>
    <div class="legend" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="legend-title">Flared+vented / production</span>
      <span class="swatch" style="--c: var(--seq-150)"></span><span>&lt;0.1%</span>
      <span class="swatch" style="--c: var(--seq-300)"></span><span>0.1&ndash;1%</span>
      <span class="swatch" style="--c: var(--seq-450)"></span><span>1&ndash;5%</span>
      <span class="swatch" style="--c: var(--seq-550)"></span><span>5&ndash;20%</span>
      <span class="swatch" style="--c: var(--seq-700)"></span><span>&gt;20%</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <main class="layout">
    <div id="map" class="map-box" role="application"
      aria-label="Top outlier units, both jurisdictions"></div>
    <aside class="panel">
      <h2 id="panel-title">Highest intensity this window</h2>
      <p class="panel-note">
        Ranked by flared+vented share of production; a unit needs
        &ge;2,000 MCF flared+vented and real production in the window
        to qualify. Click a row to locate it.
      </p>
      <table class="outliers" id="worst">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Unit</th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">MMcf</th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">%</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody></tbody>
      </table>
    </aside>
  </main>

  <p slot="footer">
    Different rules, different measurement, and both jurisdictions
    under-report against satellite observation &mdash; absolute levels
    are not a scoreboard; the comparable thing is the ratio, computed
    identically. Alberta volumes converted at 1 e3m&sup3; = 35.3147 MCF.
    Alberta: information licensed from Petrinex; data &copy; Government
    of Alberta. Texas: Railroad Commission of Texas public data.
    Non-commercial demonstration; derived statistics only.
  </p>

  <script src="../scripts/combined.js"></script>
</Base>

<style>
  .slider-wrap {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 260px;
    max-width: 560px;
  }
  .slider-wrap label {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .slider-wrap input[type="range"] {
    flex: 1;
    accent-color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
